  "experiment": "E-GSC6",
  "findings": {
    "H2_restated": "SUPPORTED, but the original phrasing was untestable as written. |D(g,g)| is FLAT WITHIN an audited LNA state and STEPS BETWEEN states, with boundaries on the audited transitions. Comparing \"transition cells\" to \"frozen-word controls\" only compares plateau membership, since a frozen-word gain sits inside whichever plateau its neighbours occupy.",
    "anchor_drift_gate": "PASS. Three epochs agree at nearly every LO with no step; worst single drift 3.99 deg (R17 4000 MHz) and 3.12 deg (R18 550 MHz), medians 0.52 and 0.43 deg. Drift is an order of magnitude too small to explain R17 high band: 0.63 deg median against 20.4 deg. See anchor_drift.json.",
    "measured_acceptance_threshold": {
      "D_gg_mae_deg": {
        "high": 2.846,
        "low": 0.925,
        "middle": 0.775
      },
      "improvement_vs_6p65_baseline": {
        "high": 2.3,
        "low": 7.2,
        "middle": 8.6
      },
      "low_band_is_a_bound_not_a_value": "R18 low band D(g,g) 0.925 deg sits BELOW its own median anchor drift of 1.08 deg, so the low-band figure and its 7.2x improvement are a BOUND. This compounds the separate low-band confound with E-HCP1 cross-arm coupling (~1 deg). Middle and high are resolved with 5.6x and 6.2x margin over median drift and stand as values.",
      "note": "this is what E-GSC6 was built to produce -- a measured threshold in place of an extrapolated one. Cross-firmware against published A; same-session A unaffected.",
      "plan_projection": {
        "high": 3.4,
        "low": 6.0,
        "middle": 5.3
      },
      "source": "R18, the untouched control unit; R17 is excluded as harness-disturbed"
    },
    "separability": "SUPPORTED. |C(g,g)| is 0.568 deg mean on R17 and 0.504 deg on R18 over 480 cells each, with no LNA-state structure. The separable per-arm model predicts the diagonal to about half a degree, so the interaction term C is at the scale of the measured 0.355-0.368 deg noise floor.",
    "tandem_premise": "SPLIT BY UNIT, and the corrected reading matters. On R18, the untouched control, H1 is SUPPORTED: |D(g,g)| is 0.925 / 0.775 / 2.846 deg for low / middle / high, comparable to or BELOW published A (0.73 / 1.24 / 3.72) in every band and far below the 6.65 deg anchored baseline. Tandem's premise holds on a healthy assembly, delivering 7.2x / 8.6x / 2.3x against that baseline versus the 6.0x / 5.3x / 3.4x the plan projected -- better than projected below 4 GHz, worse above it. On R17, whose harness has documented non-recovering connector damage, |D(g,g)| is 2-5.5x published A and 20.4 deg in the high band, three times the baseline. So the premise is NOT refuted in general; it is harness-health dependent.",
    "unit_specificity": "R17 is 5-7x worse than R18 in every band while their C values are nearly identical. R17 is the unit whose harness has had connector work and whose high-band |A| was previously driven 3.49 -> 29.41 deg without recovering; R18 is the untouched control. Absolute numbers should be taken from R18.",
    "what_tandem_does_not_do": "D(g,g) is not zero on either unit and is LNA-state structured, so tandem does not remove the gain-dependent differential phase -- it leaves D(g,g)=A(g). The residual model therefore stays REQUIRED rather than becoming a fallback. The good news is that A(g) is predictable: C(g,g) is about 0.5 deg, so a per-arm term indexed by LNA state captures it."
  },
  "firmware": {
    "attestation": "genuine -- automate RAM-loaded and regenerated the ready manifest",
